  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the Reinforcement of the Congolese Institutions in the Fight Against Illegal Trafficking of Mineral Resources &#x2013; Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the proposed project, IOM will pursue its support for the government of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) to fight against the illegal trafficking of mineral resources. The proposed third project phase seeks to consolidate the successes of the previous phases and expand the mining police approach to new targeted areas in the provinces of North Kivu (Itebero, Mangurijipa, and Goma) and South Kivu (Nzibira, Kavumu, and Bukavu areas). This will enhance the sustainability, effectiveness, and overall impact of the fight against the illegal trafficking of minerals in the DRC, strengthen the capacities of Congolese institutions in the mining approach, and improve the security situation for local communities. The project will consolidate the successes of the previous project phases by raising awareness of the key actors, disseminating the Mining Police Vademecum and the guide on prevention against SGBV and child labor in mining sites, and providing regular coaching and monitoring to the Mining Police Squadrons and the Local Security Committees (CLSPs). The project will also improve collaboration between key actors, such as the PNC, CLSPs, and CNLFM (National Anti-Fraud Commission), and community members in the intervention areas.</narrative>
  </description>
